From 7a963bc0c4886e5679a354498ad21af995dc9610 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:11:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 57/69] CUDA/HIP: single-token attention input (q/k
 norm+rope+FWHT, v FWHT, q8_0 SET_ROWS of k and v) in one launch
 (GGML_HIP_ATTN_PREP)

LFM2 attention layers with a rotated q8_0 KV cache ran, after the q/v/k matvecs, five small
kernels: rms_norm_mul_rope (q, FWHT folded), fwht (v), rms_norm_mul_rope (k), set_rows K, set_rows
V. At the q norm+rope+FWHT group, when the graph continues with the V matvec, its Hadamard MUL_MAT,
the K matvec, the k group and the two SET_ROWS, the V and K matvecs run first (unchanged MMVQ
launches) and one launch (attn_prep_f32) does the rest: blocks for the q heads and the k heads run
the code of rms_norm_mul_rope_f32 (refactored into rms_norm_mul_rope_f32_rows, shared), the k
blocks then quantize their head into the K cache as k_set_rows_quant does, the v blocks run
fwht_row_warp as fwht_cuda and quantize into the V cache. V, K and the k/v FWHT rows are read only
inside the region, so they go to pool scratch memory (the allocator may give them memory of
tensors that are dead at their graph position but read by the combined launch); any other reader
rules the fusion out. 376 -> 336 kernels per LFM2 token; attn_prep 5.9 us vs 13.1 us of kernels.

Bitwise: logit hashes of 64 greedy steps unchanged (KV q8_0 vec FA depth 0 / 3000
a3c06fe69758819e / 718efee0662e860e, kvq FA depth 0 a7ce25b73f887fed, depth 3000 b47452b9380b665b
on and off; KV q4_0 b81cc99db07e6661, q4_0 caches do not take the path).
llama-bench tg128 -r 5, LFM2.5-24B-A2B, KV q8_0, 3 rounds interleaved: 4.043 -> 3.907 ms/token.
GGML_HIP_ATTN_PREP=0: the separate launches. test-backend-ops: ATTN_PREP (new: matvecs, norm,
rope, Hadamard MUL_MATs, SET_ROWS into q8_0 caches, FLASH_ATTN_EXT) 3/3.
